    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge as our strongest play with a 77.92 score. Facing Taylor Gordon, **Carroll** benefits from a massive park boost and favorable platoon alignment, positioning him to capitalize on the scarcest category: stolen bases. Close behind is **Isaac Paredes** (68.21), whose matchup against the vulnerable Mason Barnett provides a significant ceiling, aided by an expected #3 hole placement and a massive +19% SP skill advantage. **Gabriel Moreno** also anchors the top of our lineup with a 68.51 efficiency rating; his spot in the order and a favorable park environment against a mediocre Gordon make him an elite option for daily production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley**, who yielded a respectable 61.80 score but ultimately sits behind **Josh Naylor** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**. While **Riley** is boosted by a favorable SP matchup against Brady Singer, the higher consistency and platoon profile of our active corner infielders kept him on the pine. We are also closely monitoring the pending status of **Moises Ballesteros**, **Cole Young**, and **Josh Naylor**, as all three occupy the bottom half of the projected order against Grayson Rodriguez. While **Young** and **Naylor** maintain solid scores due to Rodriguez's high xERA, any shift in the official batting order\u2014specifically moving them further down\u2014could compromise their output. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** faces a slight drag due to headwinds, and **Trevor Story** must navigate a dangerous matchup against a high-tier arm in Yordanny Espino, making him our riskiest active start. **Travis Bazzana** remains on the bench, failing to clear our 40.0 floor due to a disadvantageous L/L platoon matchup.",
